{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>To wash by the river.</b> Castrate the verse and read it: <b>and the daughter of Pharaoh went down to the river to wash in it.</b>" "<b>By the side of the river.</b> Beside the river, as in ״רְאוּ חֶלְקַת יוֹאָב אֶל יָדִי״ (II Samuel 14) — and it is literally the term for 'hand,' that a person's hand is next to it. And our Rabbis said: ״הוֹלֵךְכוֹת״ is a term of death (Sotah 12), as in ״הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי הוֹלֵךְ לָמוּת״ (Genesis 25) — they were going to die, because they protested against her; and Scripture supports this, for why do we need ״וְנַעֲרֹתֶיהָ הוֹלֵכֹת״?" "<b>Her amah.</b> Her maidservant. And our Rabbis interpreted (Sotah there): a term for 'hand.' But according to the grammatical precision of the Holy Tongue it should have been vocalized אַמָּתָהּ, with a dagesh — but they interpreted אֶת אֲמָתָהּ — her hand, and her arm stretched out many cubits."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:15.564186028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}